# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you need.
#
# Lumen runs three ways, and all three are supported:
#
#   nothing set   → Supabase if it is configured below, otherwise the
#                   Cloudflare Worker (same origin, so nothing to configure)
#   VITE_BACKEND=lumen     → Lumen's own Worker. See worker/README.md.
#   VITE_BACKEND=supabase  → the hosted backend, using the keys below
#   VITE_BACKEND=none      → local only. No account screen, no network.
#                            The reader is local-first, so this is a
#                            supported way to run it, not a broken one.
#
# The two backends hold separate data. Switching points the same local
# library at a different server; it does not migrate anything.

# VITE_BACKEND=lumen


# ── Supabase (only when VITE_BACKEND=supabase) ────────────────────────
#
# Both values come from the dashboard: Project Settings → API.

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# The anon / publishable key. It is meant to be public: every table has row
# level security, so this key can only reach rows belonging to whoever is
# signed in. Never put the *service_role* key here — that one bypasses RLS.
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key


# ── The Worker (VITE_BACKEND=lumen) ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing goes here. The Worker is served from the same origin as the app,
# so there is no URL and no key to configure — and no token in JavaScript,
# because the session is an HttpOnly cookie the browser sends by itself.
#
# Its own configuration lives in wrangler.jsonc (APP_ORIGIN, MAIL_FROM) and
# in `npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY`.
